# interplay_lifetime_texture_suspend: Two textures, each with a view, across a suspend and a resume on a fresh device. The GPU fills texture 1 blue with flags 0 and texture 2 green with invalidateGuest (2): rvg_device_finish_suspend's flush writes texture 2 back to its guest page and leaves texture 1's alone. While suspended the guest rewrites texture 1's page. The resumed device makes every object again from the guest: each texture from its page, each view from its rebuilt base. So texture 1 and its view read the guest's new bytes (the blue fill is lost) and texture 2 and its view read green. The same in every setup.
